1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,950
Lesson 14: the DK7ZB 6-element Yagi with the designer's dimensions

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:13,883
YA-NEC course, lesson 14: a published design, typed in as it is. The 6-element 2 m Yagi by DK7ZB, 28 ohm, boom 2.40 m (qsl.net/dk7zb).

3
00:00:13,933 --> 00:00:25,150
From the DK7ZB page: positions from the reflector 0 - 390 - 640 - 1150 - 1785 - 2380 mm; lengths for 10 mm elements 1017 - 971 - 935 - 907 - 905 - 876 mm.

4
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:30,017
New: an empty model. No variables this time: just numbers.

5
00:00:30,067 --> 00:00:40,369
Frequency 144.300 MHz, sweep 2 MHz to see the whole band.

6
00:00:40,419 --> 00:00:49,569
Each element is one wire across Y, from -L/2 to +L/2; X is the position on the boom. Radius 5 mm (10 mm tube), 21 segments.

7
00:00:49,619 --> 00:00:55,913
Reflector: X = 0, Y from -0.5085 to +0.5085 m (1017 mm).

8
00:00:55,963 --> 00:01:02,681
Driven element: X = 0.390, half-length 0.4855 m (971 mm).

9
00:01:02,731 --> 00:01:09,447
Director 1: X = 0.640, half-length 0.4675 m (935 mm).

10
00:01:09,497 --> 00:01:16,199
Director 2: X = 1.150, half-length 0.4535 m (907 mm).

11
00:01:16,249 --> 00:01:23,117
Director 3: X = 1.785, half-length 0.4525 m (905 mm).

12
00:01:23,167 --> 00:01:30,239
Director 4: X = 2.380, half-length 0.438 m (876 mm).

13
00:01:30,289 --> 00:01:34,773
Apply and recalculate: six elements on a 2.38 m boom.

14
00:01:34,823 --> 00:01:42,801
Feed at the centre of the driven element: w2c. Apply and recalculate.

15
00:01:42,851 --> 00:01:50,401
Result: 30.2 - j3.5 ohm, 12.06 dBi = 9.91 dBd, F/B 30.3 dB, F/R 26.4 dB, beamwidth 45 x 53 degrees.

16
00:01:50,451 --> 00:01:59,935
DK7ZB gives 9.9 dBd and 24 dB: gain agrees within 0.01 dB. His F/B is the worst rear lobe, so compare it with our F/R (26.4 dB).

17
00:01:59,985 --> 00:02:05,535
The antenna is designed for 28 ohm, not 50: set Z0 for SWR to 28 ohm.

18
00:02:05,585 --> 00:02:10,535
SWR on 28 ohm: 1.15 at 144.300 MHz.

19
00:02:10,585 --> 00:02:14,802
Frequency tab: the sweep from 143.3 to 145.3 MHz.

20
00:02:14,852 --> 00:02:23,269
SWR below 1.5 over the whole 2 MHz, gain almost flat around 12 dBi, F/B peak near 143.9 MHz: a broadband design.

21
00:02:23,319 --> 00:02:27,335
Patterns: azimuth and elevation in free space.

22
00:02:27,385 --> 00:02:34,336
Clean main lobe, side and rear lobes all below -20 dB.

23
00:02:34,386 --> 00:02:44,869
From 28 to 50 ohm DK7ZB uses a quarter-wave transformer made of two 75 ohm coax lines in parallel (37.5 ohm): see his page for the cut lengths.

24
00:02:44,919 --> 00:02:51,869
Typing a published design and checking it takes two minutes. Thanks to DK7ZB for the data. Next lesson: the same 6 elements brought to 50 ohm with the Optimizer. 73 de IC8TEM
